{
  "about": "The workspace call guard's self-test (docs/workspaces.md §2.5). Every rule in workspace-calls.json has a call it must refuse and a call it must allow. `rule` is the rule a case exercises; `by` (default: rule) is the rule the guard must name in its verdict. Values in braces come from the expectation the self-test builds from `record` with the guard's own `expect`, plus {casedir}, {fake_token} and {auth_config} (common.sh's auth_config around the fake token: the line fs_request writes), made at run time so nothing here looks like a credential. `phase` is bootstrap (before A1), ready (the default) or stopped (after a refusal). expect_refusals are records `expect` must refuse to turn into an expectation.",
  "workspace_id": "w-3f9a2c",
  "record": {
    "name": "projects/saga-agents-staging/databases/swarm/documents/workspaces/u-alice",
    "fields": {
      "tenant_id": {
        "stringValue": "u-alice"
      },
      "workspace_id": {
        "stringValue": "w-3f9a2c"
      },
      "principal": {
        "stringValue": "alice@saga.xyz"
      },
      "state": {
        "stringValue": "applying"
      }
    }
  },
